  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_033 (scvi_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) at 0.7062 acc. The RNA-only baseline with the same encoder/profile/aggregation (config_028) achieves 0.6501, leaving a 0.056 gap that conflates two factors: the image modality and the weighted fusion. With scgpt, weighted fusion improved over concat by ~0.024 (config_016 vs config_006), but we have no data on whether this holds for the richer scvi_n200 representations. Question: config_013 changes only fusion (weighted→concat) relative to config_033, isolating the fusion effect under scvi_n200. It also lets us decompose the image contribution: if config_013 is close to 0.6501, the gain is mostly from weighted fusion; if it is substantially above 0.6501, the image modality itself is adding signal. Why best next: This is a single-variable, high-information experiment that simultaneously clarifies (a) whether weighted fusion is critical with scvi_n200 and (b) how much the image encoder contributes. Under a limited budget, resolving whether to invest further in fusion design or image-encoder selection is the most consequential uncertainty remaining."
}

